# Issue #5578's design, reproduced: the advance is armed by the born rule or by
# reaching the activation's first own append; appends need no claim and no epoch
# check; no hand-off marker is consulted. With duplicate activations and foreign
# authors in the environment, an acknowledged entry is trimmed.
MODULE: NoTrimPastAckedLiveAdvance5578
TARGET: NoTrimPastAcked
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: #5578 exactly: a live advance from applied-live offsets, armed by birth or by a read position within one of the first own append, with no epoch fence and no hand-off fence
PERTURBS: Claim, OwnAppend, LiveAdvance

--- FIND
Armed(a) ==
    /\ epoch[a] > 0
    /\ rp[a] >= claimHead[a] - 1
    /\ ~hoOpen
    /\ rp[a] >= hoClosedAt - 1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: #5578's arming rule.
Armed(a) ==
    /\ mine[a] # {}
    /\ (a = "a1" \/ rp[a] >= Min(mine[a]) - 1)
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ epoch[a] > 0
    /\ epoch[a] >= shardFence
    /\ next < MaxOff
    /\ next' = next + 1
    /\ author' = [author EXCEPT ![next] = a]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no claim and no epoch check.
    /\ next < MaxOff
    /\ next' = next + 1
    /\ author' = [author EXCEPT ![next] = a]
--- END
